nt/uploads/2025/02/CO25027.pdf","title":"RSIS Commentary CO25027 on India and the Arakan Army","publisher":"RSIS","date":"2025-02","tier":2},{"url":"https://mail.dmediag.com/article/review","title":"Modi's message, Arakan's reality, and India's Myanmar gamble","publisher":"DMG","date":"2026","tier":3}]}],"stances_toward":[{"toward":"MMR","grade":"rival","trend":"stable","bond":"grievance","since":"2017-08","last_verified":"2026-10-12","confidence":"C","note":"Not a mortal enemy: Dhaka negotiates with the junta (Myanmar verified 308,797 of 828,824 names in August 2026) and with the Arakan Army, and wants return, not the end of the state. But the interests collide - 1.2 million Rohingya in Cox's Bazar, a junta that ties repatriation to the rollback of international cases and to 'security in Rakhine', the Arakan Army holding the 271 km border since December 2024 (ban on vessel movement on the Naf), and 'no new refugees will be accepted'. Crisis Group counts the junta and the AA among the actors Dhaka has to deal with; ORF (Indian view) describes the two governments as approaching the crisis 'from different directions'. The grade is our structural reading (C). Bond - grievance (2017 expulsion).","sources":[{"url":"https://asianews.network/?p=304250","title":"Can Bangladesh PM Tarique Rahman's plan break the Rohingya repatriation deadlock?","publisher":"Asia News Network","date":"2026-09-29","tier":3},{"url":"https://www.orfonline.org/expert-speak/repatriation-in-limbo-bangladesh-and-the-future-of-the-rohingya","title":"Repatriation in limbo: Bangladesh and the future of the Rohingya","publisher":"ORF (Indian think tank - Indian view)","date":2026,"tier":2},{"url":"https://www.crisisgroup.org/asia-pacific/south-asia/bangladesh","title":"Bangladesh - country page","publisher":"International Crisis Group","date":2026,"tier":2},{"url":"https://asianews.network/?p=180129","title":"Tension, fear in Teknaf as Myanmar's Arakan Army claims taking control of border with Banglades